e at all  yet after greene won his battle to find  a pitch in a caravan site he found  himself embroiled in a new struggle  green's motor insurance provider  cancelled his cover as soon as he  switched his address to a gypsy site i  phoned 54  insurance companies  and they turned me down flat  because  when they said where do you live  the address when i said a caravan saw it  no no no  um and that's all i had 54 times we  can't get insurance on our caravans  we can't get home to own contents  insurance  we can't get nothing  they sent the letter saying we canceled  your insurance because you didn't tell  us the truth where you lived  i said but i told you  it was a caravan site but you didn't  tell us it was a gypsy side  this kind of discrimination makes it  difficult to live and work the thing is  when you're traveling man you know it's  you're brought up not to just do one  thing you've got to learn  more than one job so you could be doing  roofing through work brick and  tarmacking you know you've got to learn  put your hands around everything you  know it's not just one thing in life  because everything every day  everything's getting harder unless  you've got a solid a solid performance  job  that's it  and that's that's why we  we basically  want the kids to get a good education  a good education because  our wildlife is diminishing 20 years ago  similar problem very hard for housing  association tenants to get contents  insurance for their homes they were  routinely being told we don't provide we  don't provide  the difference being there were four  million of them so eventually the  insurers thought there's a market here  we should devise a specialist product  and some of the smaller groups went into  that market and it's now quite  successfully served the problem for  gypsy travellers is that as a group  they're not as large and also they're  very marginalized in society i would  love it for a fintech company to come  along and champion their rights and say  yes  these people are just as entitled to  access financial products and insurance  as anyone else and the way that they  live their lives shouldn't be a factor  in that  accounts like greens are very familiar  to emma nuttle of friends families and  travelers a group that works against  discrimination really on every indices  gypsy and travellers face severe social  exclusion gypsum travelers have the  highest infant mortality rates the  lowest life expectancy the lowest  educational  attainment out of any groups in the uk  and financial exclusion is is another  area that yes gypsum travelers do face  a lot of our clients are homeless and  nomadic gypsies and travellers because  of the shortage of authorized sites to  stop on so they don't have a fixed  address they're statutory homeless and  it does present difficulties getting  bank accounts the client of ours went  into an insurance broker on the high  street to get insurance for the caravan  that she lived in and she had illiteracy  issues so the insurance broker filled  out the form for her and there was a  question on the form which said do you  live on a gypsy site well the broker  didn't realize that she was a traveler  and never asked the question i mean that  was an illegal discriminatory question  but  so the client didn't know that the  question was even on the form and later  down the line she had a burglary and she  went to the insurance company to pay out  and they refused her then we did  actually refer  the case to the financial ombudsman and  she won the case and she got paid  in general financial inclusion is is a  policy area where there's actually a  great deal of political consensus it's a  good thing  and there's a great deal of appetite to  do more of it you know for sort of  fairly obvious reasons right on the  labor side they see it as an issue of  you know social justice equality of  opportunity on the conservative side  they feel that you know  people you know getting that first firs